  "question": {
    "text": "In a hotel, four rooms are available. Six persons are to be accommodated in these four rooms in such a way that each of these rooms contains at least one person and at most two persons. Then the number of all possible ways in which this can be done is_____"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1080",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;persons can be distributed in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;rooms in the group of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>720</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1080</mn></math>.</p>"
